-- title:
--   Units away from varpi in the crossing model are monomials
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e$ be a natural number with $1 \le e$. Write $R =$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ (i.e. `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`) by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^{e}$, and let `const (ϖ ^ e) ϖ` denote the class in $R$ of the constant power series $\varpi$. Let $S$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $R$-algebra structure which makes it the localisation of $R$ away from `const (ϖ ^ e) ϖ`, i.e. $S = R[1/\varpi]$. Then for every $g \in S$ that is a unit there exist a unit $w$ of $R$ and natural numbers $a, b, n, k$ with $a = 0$ or $b = 0$ such that $$g \cdot \big(\text{image of } \varpi\big)^{k} = \text{image of } \big(w \cdot U(\varpi^{e})^{a} \cdot V(\varpi^{e})^{b} \cdot \varpi^{n}\big)$$ in $S$, where $U(\varpi^{e})$, $V(\varpi^{e})$ are the two distinguished elements of $R$ and the images are taken under the structure map $R \to S$. Thus, after clearing a power of $\varpi$, every unit of $R[1/\varpi]$ becomes a monomial $w\,U^{a}V^{b}\varpi^{n}$ with at least one of the exponents $a$, $b$ zero.
--
--   This is the Mazur–Rapoport description of the units on the localisation away from $\varpi$ of a crossing (the completed local ring $W[\![u,v]\!]/(uv-\varpi^{e})$ at a supersingular point of width $e$): up to a power of $\varpi$ every such unit is a monomial in $u$ and $v$, with the relation $uv = \varpi^{e}$ forcing one of the two exponents to vanish. It feeds the study of units and of the $\varpi$-adic valuations on the two branches through a crossing, and is used in [`IsLocalRing.exists_units_forall_mul_const_pow_eq_mul_monomial_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_forall_prime_mem_localization`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_units_forall_mul_const_pow_eq_mul_monomial_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_forall_prime_mem_localization).
